Package: macbook12-audio-dkms
Version: 0.3
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 000000
Depends: dkms (>= 3.0)
Recommends: linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers-cloud-amd64 | linux-headers-rt-amd64, dwarves
Suggests: linux-source-6.12, wireplumber | pipewire-audio
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: MacBook12 Audio Packaging <packaging@localhost>
Description: CS4208 audio driver for the 12" MacBook 9,1/10,1 (DKMS)
 Out-of-tree HD-audio codec driver for the Cirrus Logic CS4208 codec
 found in the 12-inch MacBook9,1 (Early 2016) and MacBook10,1 (2017).
 It replaces the in-kernel snd-hda-codec-cirrus module with a version
 that replays the macOS codec initialization sequence, enabling the
 internal speakers, headphone jack, automatic jack switching and the
 internal microphone.
 .
 Built automatically with DKMS for every installed kernel. Contains
 Debian 13 fixes for the "+deb13" kernel release naming, and bundles
 the kernel sound/pci/hda sources (6.12.115) so building does not
 require the ~1.5 GB linux-source-6.12 package; that package is
 optionally used for an exact source match when installed.
